arting edge from a face incident to the destination edge. Shortcutting the portions before and after that crossing within those two faces gives the same lower bound of 1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_183"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2001_AMC_12_Q15","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"unfold-two-faces","label":"Unfold adjacent faces","methodDirectNodeIds":{"unfold-two-faces":["cnm_051","cnm_054","cnm_185","cnm_183"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_051","cnm_054","cnm_185","cnm_183"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_139"],"id":"unfold-and-bound-all-paths","label":"Unfold two faces and prove minimality","methodDirectNodeIds":{"unfold-and-bound-all-paths":["cnm_051","cnm_054","cnm_185","cnm_183","cnm_190"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_051","cnm_054","cnm_185","cnm_183","cnm_190","cnm_055","cnm_139"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:92bce8f063c02a5ab65fed49"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 210","reason":"Drawing through C a line parallel to AD produces a triangle with sides 5,12,13. Since 5²+12²=13², its area is 30 and its height to the 13-unit side is 60/13. The trapezoid area is ((52+39)/2)(60/13)=210.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_183"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2002_AMC_10A_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"auxiliary-right-triangle","label":"Construct a 5-12-13 triangle","nodeIds":["cnm_183","cnm_177","cnm_p148"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_067","cnm_112"],"id":"solution:auxiliary-right-triangle:b746884d00fe","label":"Create a 5-12-13 triangle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"auxiliary-right-triangle":["cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_177","cnm_p148","cnm_p149"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_184","cnm_183","cnm_177","cnm_p148","cnm_p149","cnm_055","cnm_067","cnm_112"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:92bce8f063c02a5ab65fed49"],"answerChec